-- Test: section lexical scoping with shadowed names.
--
-- An unqualified name resolves to the *nearest enclosing section's* binding,
-- shadowing identically-named bindings in outer (ancestor) scopes. Names from
-- non-ancestor sections still require qualification. See
-- SECTION-LEXICAL-SCOPING-SPEC.md.

-- top-level binding
bonus MEANS 10

§ employment
salary MEANS 5000
bonus MEANS 20                  -- shadows the top-level bonus within § employment

§§ `full time`
-- `salary` is inherited unqualified from the parent § employment.
-- `bonus` resolves to § employment's bonus (20, the nearest enclosing section),
-- shadowing the top-level bonus (10).
pay MEANS salary PLUS bonus
#EVAL pay                       -- 5020

§ contractor
-- No local bonus here. The top-level bonus is an ancestor and shadows the
-- same-typed § employment binding (a non-ancestor sibling), so this resolves
-- to the top-level bonus (10).
rate MEANS bonus PLUS 5
#EVAL rate                      -- 15
-- Fully-qualified cross-section access is unchanged.
empBonus MEANS employment.bonus
#EVAL empBonus                  -- 20
